{"occurrence_no":"1708712","record_type":"occ","collection_no":"242208","identified_name":"Hybodus sp.","identified_rank":"genus","accepted_name":"Hybodus","accepted_rank":"genus","accepted_no":"34498","early_interval":"Cenomanian","max_ma":100.5,"min_ma":93.9,"reference_no":"92978","lng":"0.150000","lat":"46.755001","cc":"FR","latlng_basis":"based on nearby landmark","latlng_precision":"3","geogscale":"outcrop","geogcomments":"The Mirebeau region (Vienne, western France) has some remnants of Tertiary sediments preserved from erosion. The majority of outcrops in the region are Cretaceous and Jurassic sediments. At the place called \"Le Moulin Pochard\" there are some old open workings in a Middle Miocene (Langhian) sand lens directly eroding into a Cenomanian substrate. \"Le Moulin Pochard\" is southwest of Mirebeau, near Amberre, and coordinates based on location labeled \"Falunières de Moulins Pochas\".","environment":"marine indet.","primary_reference":"J. Biddle. 1993. Découverte d'un faunule d'âge Crétacé dans le Miocène moyen du sud-ouest du bassin de Paris. Cossmanniana, Hors-série 2:39-42","phylum":"Chordata","phylum_no":"33815","class":"Chondrichthyes","class_no":"34422","order":"Hybodontiformes","order_no":"56963","family":"Hybodontidae","family_no":"56538","genus":"Hybodus","genus_no":"34498"},
