{"occurrence_no":"2046371","record_type":"occ","collection_no":"74858","identified_name":"Hemiscyllium cf. bruxelliensis","identified_rank":"species","accepted_name":"Hemiscyllium bruxelliensis","accepted_rank":"species","accepted_no":"111364","early_interval":"Lutetian","max_ma":48.07,"min_ma":41.03,"reference_no":"93687","lng":"-1.112500","lat":"43.569721","cc":"FR","latlng_basis":"based on nearby landmark","latlng_precision":"seconds","geogscale":"outcrop","geogcomments":"Likely comes from one or several of the sites around Peyrehorade (Peyrère, La Téoulère, Poublade, Trompe, etc.), but the specific information is not given. Lin et al. (2017) mention a \"concentration horizon with shell grits, otoliths and shark teeth\" at the escarpment SE of dam, N of la Téoulère, but also screenwashing of a large sample at Trompe.","environment":"basinal (carbonate)","primary_reference":"S. Adnet, H. Cappetta, and J. Reynders. 2008. Contribution of Eocene sharks and rays from southern France to the history of deep-sea selachians. Acta Geologica Polonica 58:257-260","phylum":"Chordata","phylum_no":"33815","class":"Chondrichthyes","class_no":"34422","order":"Orectolobiformes","order_no":"34573","family":"Hemiscylliidae","family_no":"63017","genus":"Hemiscyllium","genus_no":"34585"},
