{"occurrence_no":"2046852","record_type":"occ","collection_no":"276446","identified_name":"Megasqualus orpiensis","identified_rank":"species","identified_no":"154374","difference":"recombined as","accepted_name":"Squalus orpiensis","accepted_rank":"species","accepted_no":"154373","early_interval":"Thanetian","max_ma":59.24,"min_ma":56,"reference_no":"93717","lng":"2.650000","lat":"49.577999","cc":"FR","latlng_basis":"stated in text","latlng_precision":"3","geogscale":"outcrop","geogcomments":"Somme (X = 622.650, Y = 208.750). This important sand quarry, located at the exit of Rollot, on the edge of the D27 road leading to Courcelles-Epayelles, was filled in 1993. It presented a fine section of the Thanetian over about ten meters, from the transgressive sandy levels on the chalk, up to the upper limestone levels.","environment":"coastal indet.","primary_reference":"J. Baut and B. Génault. 1995. Contribution à l'étude des élasmobranches du Thanétien (Paléocène) du Bassin de Paris. 1. Découverte d'une faune d'elasmobranches dans la partie supérieure des Sables de Bracheux (Thanétien, Paléocène du Bassin de Paris) des régions de Compiègne (Oise) et de Montdidier (Somme). Belgian Geological Survey, Professional Paper, Elasmobranches et Stratigraphie 278:185-259","phylum":"Chordata","phylum_no":"33815","class":"Chondrichthyes","class_no":"34422","order":"Squaliformes","order_no":"34536","family":"Squalidae","family_no":"81027","genus":"Squalus","genus_no":"34562"},
