{"occurrence_no":"2062230","record_type":"occ","collection_no":"278413","identified_name":"Megalolamna serotinus","identified_rank":"species","identified_no":"518841","accepted_name":"Megalolamna serotinus","accepted_rank":"species","accepted_no":"518840","early_interval":"Burdigalian","max_ma":20.45,"min_ma":15.98,"reference_no":"94364","lng":"5.157800","lat":"44.028999","cc":"FR","latlng_basis":"stated in text","latlng_precision":"4","geogscale":"outcrop","geogcomments":"The Mazan site is located in Provence (Southeastern France, 44.029044, 5.157797), the southern part of the Mormoiron Basin (Vaucluse), which is part of a succession of basins that subsided between the rising Alps and the Rhodian trough. The Malemort-du-Comtat quarry, still in operation today. Also stated as Gypsum quarry \"la Plâtrière\"’ of the company Syniat.","environment":"coastal indet.","primary_reference":"J. Pollerspöck and K. Shimada. 2024. The first recognition of the enigmatic fossil shark genus Megalolamna (Lamniformes, Otodontidae) from the lower Miocene of Europe and M. serotinus (Probst, 1879) as the newly designated type species for the genus. Zitteliana 98:1-9","phylum":"Chordata","phylum_no":"33815","class":"Chondrichthyes","class_no":"34422","order":"Lamniformes","order_no":"34598","family":"Otodontidae","family_no":"154379","genus":"Megalolamna","genus_no":"378810"},
