{"occurrence_no":"2071561","record_type":"occ","collection_no":"280042","identified_name":"Heterenchelyidarum aff. colei","identified_rank":"species","identified_no":"0","difference":"taxon not entered","early_interval":"Priabonian","max_ma":37.71,"min_ma":33.9,"reference_no":"76944","lng":"6.520331","lat":"43.959690","cc":"FR","state":"Provence-Alpes-Cote d'Azur","county":"Alpes-de-Haute-Provence","latlng_basis":"based on nearby landmark","latlng_precision":"6","geogcomments":"Topographic map 1/25,000, 3541 W, Saint-André-des-Alpes,\nx = 939.950, y = 3196.750.\nGray silty marls with nummulites (sample of about 300 kg),\nexposed in the banks of the river l’Ivoire, about 125 m SE of “La\nBastide neuve”. The upper course of the Ivoire is called “Torrent\ndes Garets”, which is the name that Boussac (1912) used instead\nof l’Ivoire, that appears on the latest 1/25,000 topographic map.","environment":"terrestrial indet.","primary_reference":"A. Girone and D. Nolf. 2009. Fish otoliths from the Priabonian (Late Eocene) of North Italy and South-East France – Their paleobiogeographical significance. Revue de micropaléontologie 52:195-218"},
